# Side effects: creation may place a real, billable call; cancellation changes state.
# Each operation needs explicit, specific authorization. Never execute all requests.
# Creation does not authorize cancellation or vice versa. Persist the original body/key before creation; send only the authorized request.
# HTTP request templates, not terminal commands or previously executed requests.
# {{...}} marks placeholders; variable substitution syntax depends on the HTTP tool.
# Bind credentials only in the host's secure configuration. Never put a real key here.
# Fixed production API; no base URL variable or environment selection is required.


### 4. Side effect: send only after this call is authorized and the original body/key are persisted
# Generate and persist {{IDEMPOTENCY_KEY}} once per logical call; keep it unchanged on retries.
POST https://api.heycall-e.com/v2/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{IDEMPOTENCY_KEY}}

{
  "phone": "<AUTHORIZED_E164_PHONE>",
  "task": "Use English. Identify yourself as an AI assistant making an authorized connection test. Ask whether the recipient can hear you clearly, allow a brief reply, and politely end the call. Do not ask for personal or financial information. Set heard_test to yes only for an explicit confirmation, no only for an explicit negative answer, and unknown when there is no clear answer. Provide a brief factual summary; do not infer an answer from silence.",
  "result_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "heard_test": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "yes",
          "no",
          "unknown"
        ]
      },
      "summary": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "heard_test",
      "summary"
    ]
  },
  "metadata": {
    "test_case": "skill-api-smoke-v1"
  }
}

### 7. Side effect: send only when the user explicitly requests cancellation of the specified call
POST https://api.heycall-e.com/v2/calls/{{CALL_RESOURCE_ID}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json
